# Phase Gates

## Gate format
No phase is complete unless all of the following are true:
1. implementation exists
2. tests exist
3. docs exist
4. validation passed
5. risks are documented

## Phase 0 gate
- repository structure created
- authoritative typed model skeletons added
- local tooling configured
- CI baseline defined
- no deprecation warnings

## Phase 1 gate
- PDF intake implemented
- page ledger implemented
- native outline extraction implemented
- native text extraction implemented
- OCR fallback implemented
- golden tests added

## Phase 2 gate
- heading detection implemented
- hierarchy builder implemented
- node span consolidation implemented
- verifier implemented
- coverage and grounding tests added

## Phase 3 gate
- provider adapter implemented
- structured-output schema path implemented
- typed validation implemented
- retry/timeouts implemented
- audit log path implemented
- malformed-output tests added

## Phase 4 gate
- workflow graph implemented
- idempotency implemented
- resumability implemented
- poison-batch path implemented
- bounded concurrency implemented
- restart/replay tests added

## Phase 5 gate
- storage schema implemented
- tree versioning implemented
- MCP read/eval/admin tools implemented
- integration tests added

## Phase 6 gate
- job submit/status APIs implemented
- tree inspection API implemented
- SSE progress stream implemented
- API contract tests added

## Phase 7 gate
- traces, metrics, structured logs implemented
- dashboards/runbooks written
- load test baseline recorded
- operational SLOs defined
- release checklist passed

